  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Steal War. Logic: See rules.',
    Player: 'War variant where players can steal cards from opponents. More strategic than classic War.',
    objective: 'Win all the cards. A player who runs out of cards during a war loses immediately.',
    gameplay: "War variant: each player has a face-down packet and a face-up capture pile. Turn your top card; higher card wins the battle and takes the cards to your capture pile (winner chooses which card goes on top). Equal cards trigger a war: three face down, one face up; higher of the face-up cards wins all. If your card's rank matches the top of an opponent's capture pile you may steal that pile instead of playing to the battle. When your packet is empty, shuffle your capture pile to form a new packet.",
    keyRules: [
      'Deck has two jokers; they are the highest cards.',
      'Won cards go on your face-up capture pile; winner may choose which new card is on top.',
      "Matching rank to opponent's pile top allows stealing that pile instead of playing to battle.",
      'Card played and released cannot be used to steal; playing a card that matches your own pile top protects your pile from being stolen that turn.',
      'Running out of cards during a war means immediate loss.',
    ],
